Fixed. Bug in `src/impl/util.js` → `padStart`. It padded the whole string including the sign, so `padStart(-50, 4)` produced `"0-50"` instead of `"-0050"` (the slice chopped off the leading zeros and left the minus in the middle). `DateTime#toISODate()`/`toISO()` therefore rendered negative years wrongly.

Fix: detect a negative input, pad the absolute value, and re-attach the `-` prefix:
```js
const isNeg = input < 0;
let padded;
if (isNeg) { padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0"); }
else { padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0"); }
return padded;
```
Verified: `padStart(-50, 4) === "-0050"`, `padStart(-5, 4) === "-0005"`, `padStart(50, 4) === "0050"`, `DateTime.fromObject({ year: -50, month: 5, day: 25 }).toISODate() === "-0050-05-25"`. Full suite unchanged at 892 passed with only the 2 pre-existing `toFormat` locale failures.
